WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.820 --> 00:00:02.540
Has Battinson been outfitted?

00:00:02.540 --> 00:00:06.640
Rumor-mongering website We Got This Covered
- a website, mind you, whose "intel" should

00:00:06.640 --> 00:00:10.410
be taken with a grain of salt - is reporting
that sources have gotten a peek at the duds

00:00:10.410 --> 00:00:14.740
Robert Pattinson will wear in the upcoming
The Batman - and if their report is accurate,

00:00:14.740 --> 00:00:18.520
it'll be a version of the Batsuit quite unlike
any we've seen onscreen before.

00:00:18.520 --> 00:00:23.110
"Why is he wearing his costume from the movie
he did 24 years ago?"

00:00:23.110 --> 00:00:26.230
"If he wore the outfit from Clean and Sober,
you wouldn't recognize him."

00:00:26.230 --> 00:00:27.230
"I'm the Batman!"

00:00:27.230 --> 00:00:29.680
No, no, not that one…

00:00:29.680 --> 00:00:33.670
This latest report falls in line with other,
independently reported rumors that The Batman

00:00:33.670 --> 00:00:38.719
will be based, at least loosely, on the Jeph
Loeb-penned limited series The Long Halloween.

00:00:38.719 --> 00:00:44.460
Published between 1996 and 1997 and featuring
art by comics great Tim Sale, the series is

00:00:44.460 --> 00:00:48.850
set in the early days of the Dark Knight's
crime-fighting career, and features Bats shaking

00:00:48.850 --> 00:00:52.670
down Gotham's criminals while investigating
a series of brutal murders.

00:00:52.670 --> 00:00:56.440
According to the report, Pattinson's Batsuit
will feature a look very similar to the one

00:00:56.440 --> 00:00:58.750
Sale created for The Long Halloween.

00:00:58.750 --> 00:01:03.239
We're talking a grey suit with traces of black,
with a large black Bat-emblem on the chest;

00:01:03.239 --> 00:01:07.480
a big, billowy blue cape with a blue cowl,
and very long, pointy ears.

00:01:07.480 --> 00:01:11.250
We can't say for sure whether this rumor is
accurate, but it does stand to reason that

00:01:11.250 --> 00:01:14.100
the look for Pattinson's Batsuit would have
been completed recently.

00:01:14.100 --> 00:01:18.490
Sure, he screen-tested in costume before landing
the role, but it's likely that the suit used

00:01:18.490 --> 00:01:22.530
for his test was from a previous production,
which is par for the course for superhero

00:01:22.530 --> 00:01:23.560
reboots.

00:01:23.560 --> 00:01:27.329
The Batman will be going before the cameras
very soon, so it's likely that its iteration

00:01:27.329 --> 00:01:30.310
of the Batsuit is at least close to being
finalized.

00:01:30.310 --> 00:01:34.020
The Batman writer/director Matt Reeves has
gone on record stating that his film won't

00:01:34.020 --> 00:01:38.530
be a straight adaptation of any one story
from the comics, but based on what he himself

00:01:38.530 --> 00:01:43.170
has said about it, it certainly seems like
The Long Halloween will be a heavy influence.

00:01:43.170 --> 00:01:47.149
Reeves has said that the flick will be a noir-ish,
gritty tale, and we know that it'll feature

00:01:47.149 --> 00:01:51.680
a pretty extensive rogues' gallery of classic
Batman villains, with Zoë Kravitz playing

00:01:51.680 --> 00:01:56.840
Catwoman, Paul Dano portraying the Riddler,
and Colin Farrell in talks to play the Penguin.

00:01:56.840 --> 00:02:00.710
That checks two boxes right off the bat, and
earlier this year, the rumor mill churned

00:02:00.710 --> 00:02:04.820
forth another nugget: that The Batman will
see the Caped Crusader investigating a series

00:02:04.820 --> 00:02:06.990
of ghastly killings plaguing Gotham.

00:02:06.990 --> 00:02:11.350
If this turns out to be accurate, and Reeves
continues to insist that his movie isn't an

00:02:11.350 --> 00:02:15.252
adaptation of any existing Batman story, then
we're going to have to go ahead and state

00:02:15.252 --> 00:02:17.300
that the director is full of it.

00:02:17.300 --> 00:02:21.720
At any rate, it would be pretty cool to get
a more comics-accurate depiction of the Batsuit.

00:02:21.720 --> 00:02:25.680
The Dark Knight's look in previous movies
has always been pretty cool, but let's face

00:02:25.680 --> 00:02:29.210
it, no previous version has had much of a
resemblance to anything we've seen in the

00:02:29.210 --> 00:02:30.210
comics' pages.

00:02:30.210 --> 00:02:31.210
"Tear resistant?"

00:02:31.210 --> 00:02:32.360
"This sucker will stop a knife."

00:02:32.360 --> 00:02:33.360
"Bullet proof?"

00:02:33.360 --> 00:02:34.800
"Anything but a straight shot."

00:02:34.800 --> 00:02:36.900
"Why didn't they put it into production?"

00:02:36.900 --> 00:02:40.500
"Bean counters didn't think a soldier's life
was worth 300 grand."

00:02:40.500 --> 00:02:45.170
From Tim Burton's Batman to Christopher Nolan's
Dark Knight trilogy, movie Batman's costume

00:02:45.170 --> 00:02:49.810
has always resembled tactical body armor modified
to look like a Batsuit more than anything

00:02:49.810 --> 00:02:50.810
else.

00:02:50.810 --> 00:02:54.260
Particularly due to the fact that The Batman
will be giving us an earlier, less experienced

00:02:54.260 --> 00:02:58.100
version of the Caped Crusader, we'd really
like to see something more in line with the

00:02:58.100 --> 00:03:01.240
classic, blue-and-grey color scheme that DC
fans love.

00:03:01.240 --> 00:03:05.600
One could make the argument that such a getup
would be a touch too reminiscent of Adam West's

00:03:05.600 --> 00:03:09.950
Batsuit from the campy '60s television series,
but we would counter that Hollywood costume

00:03:09.950 --> 00:03:15.100
designers are paid gobs of money to make superheroes
look awesome onscreen, so we probably need

00:03:15.100 --> 00:03:17.040
not worry too much about that.

00:03:17.040 --> 00:03:20.610
We'll see how it all shakes out in a year
and a half or so when the flick comes flapping

00:03:20.610 --> 00:03:23.690
into theaters on June 25, 2021.

